@page "/"

<PageTitle>LocalMetrics</PageTitle>

<div class="py-4 py-lg-5">
    <p class="text-uppercase fw-semibold text-primary mb-2">Cross-platform system monitoring</p>
    <h1 class="display-5 fw-bold mb-3">Understand your machine at a glance</h1>

    <p class="lead col-lg-9">
        LocalMetrics combines ASP.NET Core, Blazor,
        Prometheus, Docker, and NGINX. OS-specific collectors expose CPU, memory, and disk usage to a
        live dashboard and a Prometheus-compatible endpoint.
    </p>

    <div class="row g-3 my-4">
        <div class="col-md-4">
            <div class="border rounded-3 h-100 p-3">
                <h2 class="h5">Cross-platform collectors</h2>
                <p class="mb-0 text-body-secondary">Separate implementations select the appropriate metrics source for Windows, Linux, or macOS.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="col-md-4">
            <div class="border rounded-3 h-100 p-3">
                <h2 class="h5">Two ways to observe</h2>
                <p class="mb-0 text-body-secondary">A Blazor dashboard supports visual exploration while <code>/metrics</code> supports Prometheus scraping.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="col-md-4">
            <div class="border rounded-3 h-100 p-3">
                <h2 class="h5">Containerized UI</h2>
                <p class="mb-0 text-body-secondary">Docker Compose and NGINX demonstrate a small reverse-proxy topology around the local API.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="d-flex flex-wrap align-items-center gap-3">
        <a class="btn btn-primary btn-lg" href="dashboard">
            <i class="bi bi-speedometer2 me-2"></i>Open dashboard
        </a>
        <span class="text-body-secondary">Run the local API on port 5050 before opening the dashboard.</span>
    </div>
</div>
